Chapter: ListPrimFalse

 The guard on the proof normalizer's builtin-list reduction rules.
 A false ground claim about list-at must be rejected
 with the reduced value named in the mismatch (Con:5 vs Con:6). If
 this file ever compiles, the rules folded to the wrong value, or the
 unifier admitted Refl against a stuck spine; either way the guard on
 the reductions is gone.

Section: Claims

  claim bad-at : list-at (Cons 5 (Cons 6 Nil)) 1 === 5
  proof bad-at = Refl
  qed

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni "list-prim-false: should not compile"
  end
